{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"58d0cf00-62f7-43cf-9d53-1a0a4359620c","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The HR target generator has been corrected.\n\n- **Code change**: In `gen.py`, the HR corridor now uses the `start` key instead of `value` (`{ \"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi }`). This forces the Intervals export to produce an **Instant‑HR corridor**, which the watch displays as the exact BPM range rather than clamping to its own zones.\n\n- **Explanation**: The colleague’s note identified that `{value, end}` maps to zone‑based targets, causing the watch to clamp to its local zones. Switching to `{start, end}` triggers the instant‑HR mode, fixing the discrepancy.\n\n- **Applied note parts**:  \n  1. **Key rename** (`value` → `start`).  \n  2. **Target shape** (`{start, end}`) for instant‑HR corridors.  \n  3. Retaining the `%lthr` units (the original design was already correct).\n\nAll details are documented in the generated **ANSWER.md** file:\n\n[ANSWER.md](file:///Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/58d0cf00-62f7-43cf-9d53-1a0a4359620c/ANSWER.md)\n","duration_seconds":20.044985,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":10019,"output_tokens":1812,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":65344,"total_tokens":11831}}}
